# Actual Q6 asset insufficiency after two rendered candidates

This is a production blocker, not user aesthetic approval or a new asset delivery. Candidate1 and repairedcandidate2 normal Godot frames are retained. The existing stones atlas is a small isolated limestone cluster with foliage, not a connected architectural sidewall; its original production prompt explicitly says `small limestone stone cluster`, `Props isolated no ground plane, no connected scenery`. Scaling it to365–650world units makes flowers comparable to or larger than the player and does not form a credible court/well. Removing the wrongly applied atlas shader fixed vertical tails/panel edges, but did not repair this design gap. Candidate2 arch still has an exposed floating foot under the actual one-way bridge; metadata placement equality is not visual rootedness.

Required existing-style asset family, if separately authorized:

- A left broken limestone court wall and right tall remaining pier, each with an organic broken exterior edge, moss and very small flowers, enough painted resolution for300–500world height at1280x720/zoom1.60; root region connects continuously to a far rock mass or is hidden naturally behind a real bank. No grass lip implying a new standing surface. One single main arch should physically read as part of these far walls, not a ring floating over boards.
- A near-left creek rock shoulder and a more slender right receiving-bank/return silhouette in the same limestone style, with distinct shape recognizable through actual dock→island→2160bank→2280return camera projections. Transparent inner edges preserve carrier/bell/chest/telegraph and central negative space. No solid-looking cross-gap floor or support under a pass-through island.
- Painted proportions calibrated with the actual hero+UI+enemy screenshots. Foliage should read as normal-size environmental vegetation, not a giant garden. Low contrast is deliberate depth, never a substitute for credible shape. Global existing style source stays approved only within its original scope; each new combination still needs independent pixel review/user eventual acceptance.
- Exact original+derived source hashes, model/tool/reference/prompt, alpha/crop/scale/root specs, source/license status, generated file custody and real Scenery/Sprite consumer inventory. Unknown license/status remains unknown. This task did not invoke an image model or manufacture new asset provenance.

No such asset files were produced under this lease. The existing-assets-only candidate is FAILED/blocked, no new route/module/physics/input changes were used to hide the gap. Do not promote these huge-prop candidates into a final visual-quality claim. New production requires an explicitly new bounded lease and asset paths; not an in-place scope or budget change.
